  "id": "threshold-theory",
  "term": "threshold theory",
  "definition": "Threshold theory is the idea that the effects of exercise change once a certain point is crossed. In this bidirectional view, moderate exercise tends to support adaptation and health, whereas excessive exercise can lead to maladaptive or harmful responses, although people vary in where these thresholds may lie.",
